# Files copied into each new `claude --worktree <name>` checkout.
#
# A worktree starts from tracked content only, so the committed safe-default
# env files (backend/.env.development, frontend/.env.development) already travel
# with it and the stack runs out of the box. List here only the *gitignored*
# personal overrides that a session would otherwise lose — they win over the
# committed defaults (see CLAUDE.md → "No .env setup at all").
#
# NOT copied (and intentionally so): backend/.venv (hardcodes absolute paths —
# copying breaks it) and node_modules (heavy; pnpm reinstalls fast from its
# store). Run `pnpm install` / recreate the venv inside a worktree when you need
# to build or test there.
backend/.env
backend/.env.local
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local
